Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 15:04:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(frontend): persist local Manage URL history

Context:
Issue #81 (C Local uploads sidebar ADOPT_WITH_REDESIGN) requires
client-side manage-URL history on the official PasteBin UI. The gap
is in upstream-owned frontend code, so this lives on an isolated
patch branch from the pinned upstream SHA.

Expected behavior:
After a successful upload or update, the browser records the Manage
URL locally (max 50). A compact Recent uploads list on the current
index UI (not dashboard-sidebar chrome) shows public paste names.
Clicking an item fills the Manage URL field. A privacy note states
the list stays on this device. Successful delete removes that item.
Encryption keys are not stored.

Acceptance criteria:
- After upload, Recent uploads and a privacy note are visible.
- List labels do not include the Manage URL password.
- Clicking a recent item restores the Manage URL field.
- Store caps at 50 and fails closed on localStorage errors.

Constraints:
- Generic upstream patch; no Feishu concepts.
- No cloud sync, accounts, server history, analytics, or extension.
- Do not copy fork sidebar chrome.

Validation:
- TDD: RED missing Recent uploads heading / localUploads module;
  GREEN after localStorage helper + compact panel.
- Node v22.23.2 / pnpm 10.28.0
- Frontend tests: 2 files / 6 tests PASS
- lint / typecheck / Prettier PASS
- frontend production build PASS

